  "unit": "u06-bazaar",
  "title": "Please give me…",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Bengali commands change with the same three levels of 'you'. For 'give':\n\n- **দে** (*de*) — তুই (close friends, little brother)\n- **দাও** (*dao*) — তুমি\n- **দেন** (*den*) — আপনি, everyday Bangladesh\n- **দিন** (*din*) — আপনি, standard / formal (and the usual form in Kolkata)\n\n**দেন** and **দিন** are both correct and both polite. Use whichever you like; this course accepts either. (দিন is also the word for 'day', and context tells them apart.)\n\nThere is no separate word for 'please' in requests like these, because the polite verb form *is* the politeness. **আমাকে চা দিন** = 'Please give me tea'.\n\n**আমাকে** (*amake*) is 'me' as an object (compare **আমার** 'my'). **একটা** = 'one, a' (for things you count); **একটু** = 'a little' (for things you don't): **একটু পানি দাও** 'give me a little water'. **আরও** (*aro*) is 'more': **আরও একটু** 'a little more'. Don't confuse it with **আর** 'and'.\n\n**Culture:** with a shopkeeper, always use the আপনি forms, even when you call him **মামা** or **ভাই**: *মামা, একটা ডিম দেন।* Using দে with a stranger sounds rude.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "amake",
      "bn": "আমাকে",
      "tr": "amake",
      "en": "me",
      "notes": "Object form of আমি: আমাকে দেন 'give me'."
    },
    {
      "id": "den",
      "bn": "দেন",
      "tr": "den",
      "en": "give (polite)",
      "notes": "Polite imperative of দেওয়া 'give', used in everyday Bangladeshi speech. Also the present-tense 'you/he (polite) give'."
    },
    {
      "id": "din-give",
      "bn": "দিন",
      "tr": "din",
      "en": "give (polite, standard)",
      "notes": "Standard / more formal polite imperative. Same spelling as দিন 'day' — context tells them apart. Usual in Kolkata."
    },
    {
      "id": "dao",
      "bn": "দাও",
      "tr": "dao",
      "en": "give (familiar)",
      "notes": "Goes with তুমি."
    },
    {
      "id": "de",
      "bn": "দে",
      "tr": "de",
      "en": "give (intimate)",
      "notes": "Goes with তুই — only with close friends, younger siblings, small children."
    },
    {
      "id": "ektu",
      "bn": "একটু",
      "tr": "ektu",
      "en": "a little",
      "notes": "Also softens a request, like 'just': একটু দেন 'please give (me) a little'."
    },
    {
      "id": "aro",
      "bn": "আরও",
      "tr": "aro",
      "en": "more",
      "notes": "আরও = \"(even) more\"; don't confuse with আর \"and / else\". Also spelled আরো."
    }
  ],
